{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running an automated \"stitch\" task (Task ID 5615) from a code generation pipeline. The task is to implement srd106-df requirements R3.1, R3.2, R3.3, and R3.4 in the `cmd/df` package. Specifically:\n   - R3.1: `-T`/`--print-type` flag to insert a \"Type\" column after Filesystem showing filesystem type (e.g., apfs, ext4)\n   - R3.2: `-i`/`--inodes` flag to display inode information instead of block usage (columns: Filesystem, Inodes, IUsed, IFree, IUse%, Mounted on)\n   - R3.3: `-a`/`--all` flag to include pseudo-filesystems (those with 0 total blocks) in output\n   - R3.4: `-l`/`--local` flag to restrict output to local filesystems only, excluding network filesystems (NFS, SMB, CIFS, etc.)\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/df/main.go` and `cmd/df/df_test.go`. Must not modify other files. Must not run git commands. Must follow execution constitution and go style constitution exactly.\n\n   Acceptance criteria: AC1 (go build succeeds), AC2 (go vet clean), AC3 (go test passes, skips if gdf missing), AC4 (each R3.x has at least one differential test).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing against GNU reference binary `gdf` (Homebrew coreutils)\n   - Darwin-specific filesystem APIs: `unix.Getfsstat`, `unix.Statfs_t` from golang.org/x/sys/unix\n   - `unix.Statfs_t` contains: `Fstypename` (filesystem type), `Files`/`Ffree` (inode counts), `Blocks`/`Bfree`/`Bavail` (block counts), `Bsize`, `Mntfromname`, `Mntonname`\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` for differential testing\n   - `pkg/format.PadRight`/`PadLeft` for column alignment\n   - `pkg/format.HumanSize` for human-readable sizes\n   - Fixed 6-column layout using `